---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import TalkBanner from '../components/TalkBanner.astro';
import LegalDoc from '../components/LegalDoc.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import { withBase } from '../config/paths';

// Checked 2026-11-17: no Set-Cookie on any page or the enquiry endpoint, and no localStorage,
// sessionStorage or document.cookie anywhere in src/ (motion-check fails if a page stores any).
// 2026-11-23: the client area (worker/accounts/) sets one login cookie, __Host-hm_session, only
// from /api/auth/* (setup and login); worker tests check no other route sets a cookie.
---

<BaseLayout page="cookies">
  <SiteHeader slot="header" />

  <LegalDoc title="Cookie policy" updated="23 November 2026">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      The public pages of this website set no cookies. It runs no analytics, advertising or
      tracking, and stores nothing in your browser. That is why there is no cookie banner asking you
      to accept anything. The one cookie we ever set is for people who log in to their account: it
      keeps them logged in. The fingerprint button at the bottom right of every page shows this
      summary at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>What cookies are</h2>
    <p>
      Cookies are small files a website saves in your browser. Some are needed for a site to work,
      such as keeping you signed in. Others track what you do, often for analytics or advertising.
      Similar tools, such as local storage, work in much the same way, and this policy covers them
      too.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies on this site</h2>
    <p>
      On the public pages, none. We don't set cookies on any page, on the contact form or on the
      free AI check form, and we don't use local storage or similar tools. The site's fonts, images
      and videos are all served from our own domain, so no other company's content loads when you
      visit.
    </p>

    <h2>If you have an account</h2>
    <p>
      Anyone with a Hu/man account can log in to see their requests, files and portfolio. When you
      log in, we set one cookie, <code>__Host-hm_session</code>. It holds a random code that tells
      our site you're logged in, and nothing about you. It is sent only to our own site, can't be
      read by scripts on the page, and lasts 30 days or until you log out, whichever comes first. It
      is strictly necessary for a service you asked for, so under PECR it doesn't need consent. If
      you never log in, it is never set.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you pay by card from your account, you go to Stripe's own payment page (on stripe.com).
      Stripe sets its own cookies there, under its own cookie policy; none are set on our site.
    </p>

    <h2>Security cookies from our host</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted by Cloudflare. If Cloudflare's protection ever needs to check whether a
      visitor is a person or a bot, it may set a strictly necessary security cookie, such as
      <code>__cf_bm</code> or <code>cf_clearance</code>. These cookies are used only to protect the
      site. They don't track you across other websites, and they last no more than the time the
      check needs. Under the UK's Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations (PECR), cookies
      that are strictly necessary to protect a service don't need consent.
    </p>

    <h2>When you leave this site</h2>
    <p>
      Links to Instagram and to the live projects in our work take you to other websites, which have
      their own cookie and privacy policies. Those apply once you are on their sites.
    </p>

    <h2>If this changes</h2>
    <p>
      If we ever add analytics or any other cookies, we will update this policy first and ask for
      your consent wherever the law requires it.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>. How we handle
      information you send us is in our <a href={withBase('/privacy/')}>privacy notice</a>.
    </p>
  </LegalDoc>

  <TalkBanner />

  <SiteFooter slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>
